          "sentence_a": "The state is immobility.",
          "sentence_b": "The state is the quality of not moving.",
          "argumentation": "The A/B classifies the external abstract quality q, not q as a moving object. Keep the pre-enumeration LHS Immobility(q:E). The pcomp moving is a gerund nominalization of the unchanged fixed verb sense. It supplies Nom[F](h), an E-valued abstract noun referent with one optional licensed existential. Of relates q:E and h:E. The complete Move(e) AND Agent(e,s) usage stays inside Nom; the event e and formal subject s are bound only by its fixed expansion. Attached not negates existential event closure inside Nom, whereas an outer not negates the nominal/property assertion and is a different reading. Both attachments remain in the enumeration, with the single not occurrence consumed once. NominalRef/Holds are compiler-only, with no world/time dimensions in this approved version.",
